  "source_review_manifest_sha256": "sha256:092bb69a8ecc5cb04e534bbabc420806e5387f9922392cacf8c993a65f90de08",
  "body": "Cloud init now records a requested GitHub repository and named-user roster, validates that request against the local origin, and provides the hosted purchase-approval link. This recovers the unpublished billing contribution and corrects its obsolete assumption that init creates a cloud session automatically.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `--cloud-repository` and `--github-users` to both init entrypoints and preserve the normalized request in non-secret configuration.\n- Reject missing or duplicate usernames and repository/origin mismatches before writing configuration.\n- Expose the fixed approval URL; human interactive init may open it, while headless, proof, and dry-run execution only prints it.\n- Keep explicit session acquisition and backend entitlement checks authoritative. Regression coverage requires the approval link, no automatic session file, no leaked mock credential, and no readiness claim from init.\n- Update the living specifications and preserve the accepted verification, Laya, and documentation work.\n\n## Provenance and validation\n\nRecovered source: [`26a499d9`](https://github.com/DecapodLabs/decapod/commit/26a499d9f0789a5ed00605d23cfc57f5392ae8fc).\n\nExact candidate: `{{HEAD_SHA}}`.\nAccepted target: `{{BASE_SHA}}`.\n\nThe native publisher gates PR creation on complete validation of this exact candidate and target. The change does not modify CI, build definitions, or the controller contract; static patch checks are not publication proof.\n\n## Rollout boundary\n\nThis preserves the existing USD15 per named user per repository monthly purchase-intent contract. It does not deploy billing or establish that paid cloud is operational. Propodus billing deployment, GitHub admin verification, Stripe configuration and sandbox acceptance, and released client credential/route support remain prerequisites in `docs/cloud-repository-billing.md`. A roster entry or approval link cannot grant access.\n"
}
